# Legacy Jellyfin configuration. New installations use settings.example.json.
# This file is read only when settings.json has no server section.
# Blank lines and lines beginning with # are ignored.
# A server URL is enough to use Quick Connect. Approve the displayed code
# from an already signed-in Jellyfin client.
# The launcher saves login in /media/fat/misterfin-crt/state/session.json.

http://your-jellyfin-server:8096

# Optional API-key login: add the key and username after the server URL.
# your-api-key
# your-username

# Independent options can appear on separate lines anywhere in the file.
# PAL and NTSC are accepted for compatibility. Output geometry determines
# playback's frame-rate convention. These lines do not switch the CRT mode.
# NTSC

# Video conversion limits: WIDTHxHEIGHT@BITRATE (bits per second).
# Default: 720x576@12000000. Width: 160-1920. Height: 120-1080.
# Bitrate: 100000-50000000. Omitting @BITRATE keeps the current bitrate.
# Larger accepted values do not guarantee smooth playback.
# 640x480@8000000

# HTTPS verifies certificates. Prefer a trusted certificate.
# INSECURE_TLS disables verification for this server, including remote control.
# INSECURE_TLS

# DEBUGLOG enables diagnostics unless settings.json explicitly overrides it.
# Logs default to debug.log beside settings, with one rotated .1 file.
# Copy logs before restarting: each launch clears its log pair.
# Logs exclude credentials and media titles but can contain item/user IDs,
# device names, and playback timing. Review logs before sharing.
# DEBUGLOG

# Application settings belong in settings.json beside this file.
# See docs/GO_CONFIGURATION.md and docs/GO_DIAGNOSTICS.md.
